ts/test_review_brief.py::test_a_narrow_round_refuses_the_convergence_stance;tests/test_review_brief.py::test_a_convergence_brief_carries_the_stance_and_its_marking;tests/test_review_brief.py::test_a_convergence_tagged_finding_files_with_its_count_unchanged;tests/test_review_brief.py::test_the_scope_rubric_names_every_registry_the_critique_brief_renders;tests/test_plan_filing.py::test_at_the_cap_a_successor_ruling_never_passes;tests/test_review_brief_git.py::test_the_reading_scope_never_shows_a_record_of_earlier_findings;tests/test_review_brief.py::test_only_a_convergence_brief_leaves_the_decisions_record_and_critiques_out_of_its_reading_scope;tests/test_review_brief_git.py::test_an_ordinary_review_reads_the_decisions_record;tests/test_plan_filing.py::test_the_plan_critique_brief_ties_severity_to_reachability\"\n status = \"Approved\"\n phase = 6\n \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$p='\"'docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml'; \"'$s=Get-Content -Raw $p; foreach($id in '\"'171','172','260','365'){ \"'$pat='\"'(?ms)\"'^'\"\\\\[design\\\\.LLR-'+\"'$id+'\"'\\\\].*?(?=\"'^'\"\\\\[design\\\\.LLR-|\\\\z)'; [regex]::Match(\"'$s,$pat).Value };'","aggregated_output":"[design.LLR-171]\nsr_refs = [\"SR-035\"]\ntitle = \"Language-neutral registry templates + ID scheme\"\nmodule = \"project-trajectory/registries\"\ncode_symbol = \"registry templates / ID vocabulary\"\ndetail = \"\"\"The shipped registry templates and the ID scheme (SN/SR/LLR/TC and the off-spine spaces) carry no language-specific token: a scaffold produced with a non-Python profile passes trace.py --strict-integrity --strict-schema unmodified, and a token scan over the shipped templates and the ID vocabulary finds no language-specific token.\"\"\"\nrationale = \"\"\"Stack-agnosticism was a real delivered property with no observable; this is the check that makes it falsifiable.\"\"\"\ntest_refs = \"(see TC-165)\"\nstatus = \"Approved\"\ncomponent = \"CMP-009\"\nphase = 1\n\n\r\n[design.LLR-172]\nsr_refs = [\"SR-165\"]\ntitle = \"Component derivation record: element completeness + the ranking recompute\"\nmodule = \"project-trajectory/scripts/trajectory_arch.py\"\ncode_symbol = \"component_findings\"\ndetail = \"\"\"Extends the existing component pass — the one home that already reads docs/requirements/components.toml and already emits CMP findings — with the derivation-record rules SR-165 states, rather than adding a second reader of the same registry. Per live CMP row: the record must declare the candidate partitions considered, the objective and the constraints they were scored against, a score per candidate, the selected partition, and the human ruling that named the components and adopted it; a missing element is one finding naming the row AND the element. Two derived rules on top of presence, because presence alone is satisfiable by a record that says nothing: (1) THE RANKING RECOMPUTES — re-rank the recorded candidates from the record's own objective, constraints and scores and compare with the recorded order, a mismatch being a finding, which is what makes the record falsifiable without a reviewer re-running a model session; (2) A SELECTION THE SCORES DO NOT RANK FIRST is a finding unless the record carries a human override naming that choice, so a legitimate \"the scores said A, the human chose B\" is expressible and an unexplained one is not. Vacuous by construction on a project declaring no components, and on the example -000 rows. NOT BUILT YET: the record cells do not exist on the CMP schema today — recorded as open debt on this row and TC-166; SR-165 carries Test verification precisely because the check is mechanizable, and this is the debt that verification incurs, recorded rather than silently owed.\"\"\"\nrationale = \"\"\"The check belongs where component_findings already is for the reason the census keeps applying: a second module reading components.toml would be a second answer to \"is this partition recorded\", and the two would drift. The recompute is the load-bearing half — an element-presence check passes on a record whose scores contradict its own conclusion, which is the exact failure SN-040 exists to catch (the next reviser cannot tell load-bearing boundaries from accidents). The override arm is what stops the recompute rule from forbidding human judgement: the requirement is that a departure from the scores is RECORDED, never that it is disallowed.\"\"\"\ntest_refs = \"TC-166\"\nstatus = \"Approved\"\ncomponent = \"CMP-006\"\nphase = 5\n\n\r\n[design.LLR-260]\nsr_refs = [\"SR-157\"]\ntitle = \"An approved test case's tier agrees with where its evidence runs\"\nmodule = \"project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/spine.py\"\ncode_symbol = \"evidence_items/tier_findings\"\ndetail = \"\"\"evidence_items(cell) reads a test case's Evidence cell as (path, node) pairs: items separated by `;` or whitespace outside a node's bracketed parametrization, a `path::node` id kept whole with its parametrized suffix, spaces inside the brackets included, a parenthetical note dropped and a `#anchor` read as its document. tier_findings(tcs, tier_of) judges only Approved test cases, taking the tier a path runs in from tier_of(path), which answers \"smoke\", \"slow\" or None for a path that is no test the harness runs: a case whose Tier is Smoke and none of whose evidence runs in the smoke tier is an error naming the case and its evidence paths, and a case whose Tier is Full and none of whose evidence is slow is an advisory in the same shape, never an error; a Release case and a case below approval are silent. This repository binds tier_of to its test-module tiering in a test of the per-commit tier, so an error fails the commit bar.\"\"\"\nrationale = \"\"\"SR-157 asks the harness to report every declared spine rule violation naming the at-fault row and cell, gating the declared failure set while advisory classes never change the exit code. A test case's Tier cell is such a rule: an approved Smoke case whose evidence runs only at close claims a per-commit run that does not happen, and nothing checked it, so evidence moved to a slow module left the cell false and a stale pin in that module unseen until a close run. The error names the case and its evidence and gates; the Full-side disagreement understates rather than falsifies, so it stays advisory. Which tier a test runs in is the harness's answer, which the kit cannot read in a stack-neutral way, so the rule is pure over a tier function the project binds. The Evidence cell's reading sits in this row because the rule is its first reader; the module listing reads the same cell through it.\"\"\"\nstatus = \"Approved\"\ncomponent = \"CMP-006\"\nphase = 6\n\n\r\n[design.LLR-365]\nsr_refs = [\"SR-157\"]\ntitle = \"Test-file declarations of their test cases\"\nmodule = \"project-trajectory/scripts/gen_arch_map.py;project-trajectory/scripts/trajectory_arch.py\"\ncode_symbol = \"read_test_tags/tc_tag_findings\"\ndetail = \"A test-file back-link declaration names test cases, and each named id must be a live test case. In a Python test file, declarations in the module docstring and in a test's docstring are read; in another supported test-file type, declarations are read at file level. A byte-order mark at the start of a file does not change its reading. The two Python levels union. A test repeating its module's test case is no finding. A non-docstring string literal, a backtick-quoted token and an unsupported test-file type make no declaration. A declaration outside a read position, including a pytest-fixture docstring, is refused as misplaced. The following are refused as malformed: a declaration whose list is not test-case ids only; a read-position line whose token follows prose and names a test case; and a next line that continues a valid list. The after-prose refusal directs the declaration to the start of its own line. An id absent from the live test-case registry, including an example or retired id, is refused as unknown; a Drafted test case is live. A test file that cannot be decoded or parsed is refused as unreadable. Every live id in a valid declaration maps to its test node. Each refusal names the repository-relative file, line and shape. Reading test files does not change source-file declaration reading. An absent tests root, or an absent test-case registry, makes the check vacuous. Findings warn without strict checking and error under strict checking; they gate from DevStg-Impl and remain warnings below that rung, including in a newly created project. The contract covers test files, test-case registries and declared tests roots produced by supported workflows; non-Python fixture text, non-default test-collection patterns, hand-chosen test-case aliases and tests roots reached through a symlink are outside it.\"\nrationale = \"A tag that is silently misplaced, malformed, dangling or unreadable can make a test case appear absent without an attributable finding. Keeping the declaration grammar separate from source-file reading prevents this added input from changing established source analysis.\"\ntest_refs = \"TC-404; TC-405; TC-406; TC-407; TC-408; TC-409\"\nstatus = \"Approved\"\ncomponent = \"CMP-006\"\nphase = 6\n\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$p='\"'docs/requirements/interfaces.toml'; \"'$s=Get-Content -Raw $p; [regex]::Match($s,'\"'(?ms)\"'^'\"\\\\[interface\\\\.IF-263\\\\].*?(?=\"'^'\"\\\\[interface\\\\.|\\\\z)').Value; \"'$p='\"'docs/requirements/components.toml'; \"'$s=Get-Content -Raw $p; [regex]::Match($s,'\"'(?ms)\"'^'\"\\\\[component\\\\.CMP-006\\\\].*?(?=\"'^'\"\\\\[component\\\\.|\\\\z)').Value\"","aggregated_output":"[interface.IF-263]\nowner = \"scripts/trajectory_arch\"\nrequestors = [\"scripts/check_trajectory\"]\nchannel = \"call\"\ndata = \"architecture inventories and findings for seams, contracts, components, code symbols, spec boundaries, and test-file tags\"\nversion = \"v1\"\nstatus = \"Drafted\"\ncomponent = \"CMP-006\"\n\n\r\n[component.CMP-006]\nname = \"W1 Registry & conformance\"\ncategory = \"software\"\nknowledge = \"registry-hygiene\"\nstatus = \"Approved\"\nnotes = \"\"\"The spine and everything that decides whether it holds: spine_carrier, trace, trace_text, spine_rules, check_trajectory, plan_coverage, migrate_carrier, wi_convert, gen_arch_map. The shared helper package kitlib (config.py/git.py/registry.py/__init__.py via LLR-181, ladder.py via LLR-184, stage.py via LLR-185, evidence.py via LLR-192, spine.py via LLR-197, secret_classes.py via LLR-205) is owned here alone, single-tagged CMP-006 - the closest-fit reason is registry.py's bulk within LLR-181's module set. It is still imported from every component; that consumption is recorded on a declared shared-kernel surface (docs/kernel-modules-allow) rather than by a multi-tag - a single `Component` cell can no longer silence a genuine cross-component seam finding. kitlib/station.py (LLR-182) and kitlib/verdict.py (LLR-207) are the package modules NOT owned here: both stay CMP-008, each one's cross-component edges declared and policed as an interface row - IF-093 for the station, IF-175 for the verdict record - rather than folded into the kernel surface. gen_arch_map also carries a CMP-009 tag through LLR-080, the one LLR row whose modules straddle this cut - its single import edge stays POLICED (IF-117 covers it), so no seam is suppressed.\"\"\"\n\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
